  "avatar_acceleration": "Locally built optional FPS native extension from the filtered districts integration; same binary for every renderer. Not a portable release build.",
  "measurement_notes": [
    "120 warmup and 360 sampled frames per case, uncapped and vsync disabled. No screenshot/readback within the sampled interval.",
    "Wall-clock frame time is the primary whole-client metric. Viewport GPU time and custom column dispatch GPU time are separate measurements; neither viewport time alone nor a sum of percentile values is whole-frame GPU latency.",
    "32-rig cases use 32 animated shared copies of one bundled VRM per case, production distance LOD, springs disabled, four rows at 12\u201318m camera depth. No unique-avatar, networking, combat or XR certification.",
    "Terrain and factory use unshaded colors. Factory collision/gameplay integration is not implemented. Columns march to 250m with yaw-only projection; the raster camera far plane is 300m.",
    "Static front cases repeat in reverse order; 32-rig renderer comparisons are one sequence per model and show appreciable host/animation timing variation. Do not interpret small differences as a reliable terrain ranking under avatar load.",
    "The BSP case uses different content/materials/sky and runs last; it is context, not an equivalent-content replacement comparison."
  ]
}
